# UI

- React Server Components by default. Add `'use client'` only for browser APIs, local state, effects, or event handlers.
- Keep data access and authorization on the server. Do not fetch privileged rows in client components.
- Reuse `src/components/ui/` (button, input, textarea, dialog, dropdown, card, badge, label, skeleton, separator) before adding primitives.
- Public chrome: `src/components/site/`. Studio: `src/components/studio/`. Prose: `src/components/prose/`. SEO: `src/components/seo/`.

## Reading product

- Typography-first. Measure content at `max-w-prose` (68ch). Warm paper/ink tokens in `globals.css`.
- Dark mode is a `html.dark` class toggle (`ThemeToggle` + inline init script). Do not switch to `prefers-color-scheme` media as the only mechanism.
- Preserve semantic HTML, headings, labels, focus, and contrast. Long-form reading beats dashboard chrome.

## Quality

- Pending/busy feedback on every async submit (disable, spinner or label, `aria-busy`). Block double-submit.
- Keep client props narrow and serializable. Do not pass Supabase clients or secret-bearing objects to the client.
- Match adjacent loading, empty, and error patterns. Do not invent a second visual system.

New screens or redesigns: `design` skill.
